       			<div class="video-area" id="feature-benefit-half-text-video-container-uniq-id-3706493f-9315-4526-99ed-3bb9dd159722_root_responsivegrid_pd_g_feature_benefit_1344793689">
		           <div class="video-area__inner">
		               <div class="video" data-image-default="false" data-video-embed="false" data-video-type="youtube" data-video-data='{
				           "id": "i4vjmfBuPeI",
				           "title": "How to use Vascular Load | Galaxy Watch8 Series",
				           "caption": "Text in the middle: How to track your Vascular Load with Galaxy Watch8. New text appears: Monitor your Vascular Load and easily gain insights into your heart health. New text appears: Let&#39;s get started. Scene changes, text appears at the top: First, pair your watch with your phone. Galaxy Watch8 Classic and smartphone appear from left and right. New text appears: Tap &#39;Connect&#39;. Galaxy Watch8 screen displays text Welcome and smartphone screen displays a popup with Galaxy Watch8 Classic turning 360 degrees. Text Galaxy Watch8 Classic, A new device has been detected. At the bottom are buttons Cancel and Connect. Connect button is tapped. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Scene changes. Galaxy Watch8 Classic on the right. On the left, text appears: Swipe all the way to the left to add the tile. Galaxy Watch8 Classic screen is swiped and plus button with text Add tiles appear. On the left, new text appears: Tap &#39;Add tiles&#39;. Screen on Galaxy Watch8 Classic is tapped. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Add tiles feature is onscreen. On the left, new text appears: Tap &#39;Vitals&#39;. Galaxy Watch8 Classic screen is scrolled down. Vitals is tapped. Vascular load feature appears. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. On the left, new text appears: Select &#39;Vascular load&#39;. On Galaxy Watch8 Classic, Vascular load is tapped. Text Heart, Vascular load icon, text Vascular load and plus button is onscreen. Vascular load is tapped and displayed onscreen. On the left, new text appears: Tap &#39;Show on phone&#39;. Galaxy Watch8 Classic screen is scrolled down and Show on phone button is tapped. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To measure vascular load, it is required to wear Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch Ultra, Watch8 and later released Galaxy Watch series) when sleeping for at least 3 days out of recent 14 days. Vascular load monitoring is for fitness and wellness purposes only. If you’ve been diagnosed with cardiovascular disease or are recovering from surgery, be sure to follow your doctor’s treatment plan. This is a Labs feature that you can preview before its official launch. If you don&#39;t want to use this experimental feature, you can turn it off in Samsung Health settings. Scene changes. On the right, smartphone with Vascular load feature onscreen with Next button at the bottom. On the left, text appears: Now you&#39;re good to go! Next button on smartphone screen is tapped. Page explaining vascular load is onscreen. Get started button is at the bottom. Screen is scrolled down and Get started button is tapped. Baseline feature is onscreen. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To measure vascular load, it is required to wear Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch Ultra, Watch8 and later released Galaxy Watch series) when sleeping for at least 3 days out of recent 14 days. Vascular load monitoring is for fitness and wellness purposes only. If you’ve been diagnosed with cardiovascular disease or are recovering from surgery, be sure to follow your doctor’s treatment plan. This is a Labs feature that you can preview before its official launch. If you don&#39;t want to use this experimental feature, you can turn it off in Samsung Health settings. Scene changes, text in the middle: Ready to start monitoring? New text appears: Just have your watch on for 3 nights during sleep. Above are 3 Vascular Load icons that are marked to indicate 3 nights have passed. Scene changes. On the left, text appears: And your baseline will be ready. On the right is smartphone with Vascular load feature onscreen, displaying the baseline setup process is complete. Screen changes to show Steady vascular load. On the left, new text appears: Now you can track your vascular load with your watch! On the smartphone, graph icon is tapped. On the left, new text appears: Keep track of your heart while you sleep. On the smartphone, different 7 day-records of vascular load appear, showing Steady and Higher vascular load graphs. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To measure vascular load, it is required to wear Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch Ultra, Watch8 and later released Galaxy Watch series) when sleeping for at least 3 days out of recent 14 days. Vascular load monitoring is for fitness and wellness purposes only. If you’ve been diagnosed with cardiovascular disease or are recovering from surgery, be sure to follow your doctor’s treatment plan. This is a Labs feature that you can preview before its official launch. If you don&#39;t want to use this experimental feature, you can turn it off in Samsung Health settings. Scene changes. On the right is Galaxy Watch8 Classic with Vascular load feature onscreen. Vascular load is Lower with bar graph below and the Vascular Load icon at the left to illustrate the vascular load is low. On the left, text appears: If your vascular load is low,. New text appears: it means your diet, activity and stress are in balance. On Galaxy Watch8 Classic, Vascular Load icon on bar graph moves towards the right and the text above changes accordingly to Slightly lower to Steady. On the left, new text appears: If your vascular load is high,. On Galaxy Watch8 Classic, Vascular Load icon on bar graph moves further towards the right and the text above changes accordingly to Slightly higher and Higher. On the left, new text appears: it may signal poor diet, inactivity or high stress. Galaxy Watch8 Classic screen is scrolled down and Show on phone button is onscreen. Show on phone button is tapped. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To measure vascular load, it is required to wear Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch Ultra, Watch8 and later released Galaxy Watch series) when sleeping for at least 3 days out of recent 14 days. Vascular load monitoring is for fitness and wellness purposes only. If you’ve been diagnosed with cardiovascular disease or are recovering from surgery, be sure to follow your doctor’s treatment plan. This is a Labs feature that you can preview before its official launch. If you don&#39;t want to use this experimental feature, you can turn it off in Samsung Health settings. Scene changes. On the left, text appears: Get tips on how to develop a healthier lifestyle. On the right, smartphone with details on vascular load, such as sodium intake and lifestyle information. Screen is scrolled up to show the top part of Vascular load feature screen. Vascular load is Steady. On the left, new text appears: Stick to a healthy routine to keep your vascular load steady. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Sequences shortened. Actual UI may be different. Vascular Load available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires the Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To measure vascular load, it is required to wear Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch Ultra, Watch8 and later released Galaxy Watch series) when sleeping for at least 3 days out of recent 14 days. Vascular load monitoring is for fitness and wellness purposes only. If you’ve been diagnosed with cardiovascular disease or are recovering from surgery, be sure to follow your doctor’s treatment plan. This is a Labs feature that you can preview before its official launch. If you don&#39;t want to use this experimental feature, you can turn it off in Samsung Health settings. Scene changes, text appears in the middle: Manage your Vascular Load to stay balanced. Scene changes. Galaxy Watch8 Classic is on its side and is slightly turned. Galaxy Watch8 appears in a slightly tilted front view and is placed next to Galaxy Watch8 Classic. Text Galaxy Watch8 Watch8 Classic. Scene changes. In the middle, samsung.com. Samsung logo.",
						   "muted": false,
				           "autoplay": false
				        }'>
		               </div>
		             
		               
					  
					   
					
					  		
